# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
# Optional. Without either of these the simulator runs in scripted mode, no AI needed.
# Claude on Amazon Bedrock: set the region. AWS credentials come from the normal AWS chain
# (an IAM role when hosted, or `aws configure` on a laptop). Never put AWS keys in this file.
# MG_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1
# Or the Claude API:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional. Model to use (default claude-opus-5-5) and, on Bedrock, the model used if it declines (default claude-opus-4-8).
# MG_MODEL=
# MG_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# Optional. Email the trusted contact through Amazon SES when a request is waiting. All five are needed.
# In the SES sandbox, both addresses must be verified. Demo visitors (?demo=...) never trigger email.
# MG_SES_REGION=us-east-1
# MG_EMAIL_FROM=guardian@your-verified-domain.example
# MG_FAMILY_EMAIL=anna@example.com
# MG_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-hosted-address.example
# MG_LINK_SECRET=  (a long random string; signs the links in the email and the OAuth tokens)
# Optional. Alexa+ sign-in (OAuth 2.1). Off unless all of these and the two above are set; then /mcp needs a token.
# Copy the client ID and secret into the Alexa developer console, and register every redirect URI it lists.
# MG_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# MG_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=  (a long random string)
# MG_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS=https://alexa.amazon.co.jp/...,https://layla.amazon.com/...,https://pitangui.amazon.com/...
# MG_HOUSEHOLD_PASSCODE=  (asked once, when the family links the skill in the Alexa app)
# MG_OAUTH_STORE=  (where refresh tokens are kept, hashed; default oauth.json next to the ledger)
# Sent to FINRA, SEC, TreasuryDirect and FDIC so they can see who is calling. Put a contact in it.
# MG_USER_AGENT=MoneyGuardian/0.1 (contact: you@example.com)
# PORT=8790
